  "skill_summaries": {
    "ultimate": "deal multiple rapid damage hits to the enemy",
    "skill1": "mark the top attacker and top damage-taker as priority targets",
    "skill2": "attack target twice",
    "skill3": "battle ATK speed increase",
    "skill4": "debuff adapts to enemy combat role",
    "skill5": "enhanced damage against marked enemy roles"
  },
  "play_overview": "[[Sinbad]] marks the top attacker and top damage-taker, then focuses fire on those roles with **enhanced damage against marked targets**. His ultimate delivers multiple rapid hits to one target for concentrated burst pressure. A follow-up skill attacks twice, while his debuff adapts to the enemy's combat role on each mark. Battle ATK SPD growth keeps his rotation moving through longer fights. He shines when a clear carry can be isolated, but evenly distributed damage or mark-immune lines deny much of his priority targeting.",
  "counter_overview": "[[Sinbad]] marks the highest attacker and highest damage-taker, then adapts debuffs and rapid hits to those roles. Spread damage and avoid presenting one isolated carry; the marks are strongest when both land on the same target. His movement makes pin-burst unreliable, so use lasting coverage like [[Shemira]] or [[Frieren]] and inhibit the marked carry with [[filter:backline-inhibit]] like [[Bonnie]] or [[Evie]]. Race the mark cycle with [[filter:energy-provider]] like [[Thador]] or [[Hugin]]."
